pocket-motion-only: a bloom is a filter-layer composite (0018), drawn by this rasteriser only; no upstream target draws filter layers.

0033 — `glow-mode-luma`: a glow made from the bright pixels (a bloom).

A `glow-*` is CSS's drop shadow at offset 0: made from the layer's ALPHA,
tinted and blurred, under the content. That is right for a drop shadow and
wrong for light. An 85 % dark plate (#0b0b0b) in a white glow layer has a
white halo under its whole area, 15 % of it shows through, and the plate
reads LIGHTER than the ground — where a neon or HUD film wants light
emitted by its bright pixels only.

`glow-mode-luma` makes the same glow from the layer's own premultiplied
colour, weighted per pixel by how far its brightest channel is above
`glow-threshold-[t]` (0..1, default 0.5): 0 at the threshold, 1 at full.
That emission is offset, blurred with the same passes, multiplied by the
gain, tinted by the glow colour (white keeps each pixel's own colour), and
ADDED over the composited content — the `plus-lighter` blend, which never
darkens. A pixel at or below the threshold emits nothing, so the dark
plate comes out exactly as with no glow, while a white rule on it glows
white and a cyan bar glows cyan. `glow-mode-alpha` is the default and says
so.

Encoding: no new op and no new word. LAYER_PUSH's blend word carries the
blend mode in bits 0-7, GlowMode in 8-15 and, for Luma, the threshold x 255
in 16-23; an alpha glow leaves the upper bits 0, so every existing draw
list is word for word what it was. PROP `glowMode` = 185 (enum `GlowMode {
Alpha: 0, Luma: 1 }`) and `glowThreshold` = 186 (f32), neither animatable;
the radius, colour and gain are the glow's own `dropShadow*` props, which
still animate.

Guard: `a_luma_glow_lights_the_bright_pixels_and_leaves_a_dark_plate_dark`
(`engine/core/src/tests.rs`): over a mid-grey ground, the 85 % plate in an
alpha glow is lighter than with no glow (the case); in a luma glow it is
byte-identical to no glow; a white 2 px rule on it gains a halo on the
plate and past its edge, and no pixel anywhere is darker. Red with the
luma flag ignored (the plate in a luma glow came out lighter), green with
it. `validate_drawlist` holds the blend word's fields. `tests/tailwind.test.ts`
pins the compiler; `compositions/bloom` is the fixture, an alpha glow and a
luma glow side by side on the same plate.

Ledgers, against the same tree without this patch: no existing digest and
no existing `visibility` row moves — an alpha glow's words and pixels are
what they were. `compositions/bloom` is new in both: 2 frames, 6 named
nodes, all shown.

